# Agentic Workspace — Cursor (Unified, Ticket-Folder Workflow)

> Cursor always-on project context (equivalent role to root `CLAUDE.md` for Claude Code).
> Canonical SDD source lives under `agentic/`; install with `scripts/setup-agentic.sh cursor`.
> Project overlays (`bcs-*`) stay in IDE runtime dirs and are **outside** the required orchestrator.

## Workspace Identity

Company-wide Agentic Workspace for spec-driven (SDD) development with self-healing review loops — staged and gated, not free-form chat. GSD (thin vertical slices) keeps each implementation phase small and independently testable.

**Core principle:** Agents write code and configuration. Agents never deploy. Deployments are CI/CD only. Code ships through GitLab MRs.

**One control-file convention:** every ticket folder has exactly `_state.json` + `_notes.md` — never `context.json`. Required orchestrator `/run` starts at `/prd` → `/spectech` → `/tasks` (no `/plan`, no single-`spec.md` mode). Folder/schema contract: project skill `bcs-ticket-workflow` (`.agents/skills/bcs-ticket-workflow/`).

## Where things live (Cursor)

| Kind | Path |
|------|------|
| Subagents / personas | `.cursor/agents/` |
| Framework skills | `.cursor/skills/` |
| Project overlays | `.agents/{agents,commands,skills}/bcs-*` (Cursor skills load from here; agents and commands are linked into `.cursor/`) |
| Hooks | `.cursor/hooks.json` + `.cursor/hooks/` |
| Canonical source | `agentic/` (edit here, then re-run setup) |

## Personas

Invoke via Task / agent defs under `.cursor/agents/`, or slash skills where present (e.g. `/run` → `.cursor/skills/run`).

| Trigger | Role | Agent |
|---------|------|-------|
| /prd | Product Requirements | `prd` |
| /spectech | Technical Designer | `spectech` |
| /tasks | Task Specialist | `tasks` |
| /dev /sre /data | Implementers | `dev` / `sre` / `data` |
| /qa | QA & Security | `qa` |
| /fix /do | Debugger / Ad-hoc | `fix` / `do` |
| /summary /scrum /kb | Summary / PO-SM-PM / KB | `summary` / `scrum` / `kb` |
| /run | Pipeline orchestrator | *(no agent — main loop + `run-pipeline` skill)* |
| /clone /rebase /kb-refresh /kb-concentrator /setup-workspace | Utilities | skill |

`scrum` is read-only. Personas escalate helpers/MCP with `REQUEST_MAIN:` / `QUESTION:` / `APPROVAL_NEEDED:` — only the **main loop** schedules `Task(...)`.

## Ticket folder

```
docs/specs/{YYYY-MM-DD}-{TICKET-KEY}-{slug}/   # or without ticket key
├── _state.json   # ONLY machine control file
├── _notes.md
├── prd.md / spectech.md / tasks.md
├── qa-report.md / summary.md / …
```

**Orchestrated `/run`:**  
`Task(prd)` → `Task(spectech)` → `Task(tasks)` → plan-reviewer → scrum → implement phases → reviewers + security-scanner + scrum → qa → scrum → summary → Finish.

Never merge `prd`/`spectech`/`tasks` into one `spec.md`.

## Flat orchestration

Subagents must not nest Task. Main session only. `/run` follows `.cursor/skills/run-pipeline/SKILL.md`.

## Multi-repo

Child repos are subdirs of the workspace root (gitignored). Add with `/clone`. Inventory is injected by `session-init`. Use `[domain:repo]` tags and phases for cross-repo work. `subagent-gate` blocks writes when a child repo is on `main`/`master`/`develop`/`release/*`.

## Knowledge / MCP

Prefer ARC MCP when configured; else `knowledge/{project}/`. Enterprise MCP only via main-loop `Task(mcp-*)` after `REQUEST_MAIN:` — personas never call enterprise MCP directly.

## Error highlights

Missing ticket folder → search `docs/specs/`. Two control files (`context.json` + `_state.json`) → stop (AC-1). Hook failures fail-open except protected-branch writes (always refused).
